-- title:
--   Lemma 2, p.8 — $e^{-4\Delta}\le \Pr[t_i\in\mathcal E\wedge t_{-i}\in\mathcal E']/(\Pr[t_i\in\mathcal E]\Pr[t_{-i}\in\mathcal E'])\le e^{4\Delta}$
-- statement:
--   Let $t$ be generated by a Markov random field with maximum weighted degree $\Delta$. For every item $i$, every set $\mathcal E\subseteq T_i$ and every set $\mathcal E'\subseteq T_{-i}$,
--
--   $$
--   e^{-4\Delta}\,\Pr[t_i\in\mathcal E]\,\Pr[t_{-i}\in\mathcal E']\;\le\;\Pr[t_i\in\mathcal E\wedge t_{-i}\in\mathcal E']\;\le\;e^{4\Delta}\,\Pr[t_i\in\mathcal E]\,\Pr[t_{-i}\in\mathcal E'].
--   $$
--
--   The joint law of $(t_i,t_{-i})$ is within a factor $e^{\pm4\Delta}$ of the product of its marginals on every rectangle. It is used to bound Tail, Single and the covariances of the truncated values.
--
--   **Formalization Note** $t_{-i}$ is the restriction of $t$ to the items other than $i$, and $\mathcal E'$ is a set of such restrictions.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - reading: item values t_i of unspecified sign (Def 1: 'interpret ti as the value of item i') → values in ℝ≥0; reason: the proofs use t_i ≥ 0 throughout (Lemma 22 drops π_i ≤ 1 against t_i, Lemma 7 uses c_i c_j ≥ 0, Theorem 2 uses C ≤ Σ t_i); item values are nonnegative in this literature
--   - reading: alphabets Σ_v / type space T of unspecified cardinality → finite alphabets (Finset), finite support; reason: Def 4 takes a max over all configurations and every sum of the paper ranges over a finite T; the duality benchmark [14] is for finite type spaces
--   - encoding: the ratio Pr[t_i∈ℰ ∧ t_{−i}∈ℰ′]/(Pr[t_i∈ℰ]·Pr[t_{−i}∈ℰ′]) lies in [e^{−4Δ}, e^{4Δ}] → the two inequalities multiplied out by Pr[t_i∈ℰ]·Pr[t_{−i}∈ℰ′]; reason: equivalent for nonempty ℰ, ℰ′ (the MRF has full support); for an empty set the ratio is 0/0 and the multiplied form holds trivially
-- source:
--   Cai & Oikonomou, On Simple Mechanisms for Dependent Items, arXiv:2106.10814v2, Lemma 2, p.8 (PDF 9)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_SimpleMechMRF_TypeDist
import Definitions.Def_SimpleMechMRF_MRF

open scoped NNReal

namespace SimpleMechMRF

/-- **Lemma 2** (Cai & Oikonomou, *On Simple Mechanisms for Dependent Items*,
arXiv:2106.10814v2, p. 8, PDF 9). Let `t` be generated by an MRF `G` with law `D` and maximum
weighted degree `Δ`. For any item `i`, any set `ℰ ⊆ Tᵢ` and any set `ℰ' ⊆ T₋ᵢ` (a set of
vectors indexed by the other items),
`e^{−4Δ} · Pr[tᵢ ∈ ℰ] · Pr[t₋ᵢ ∈ ℰ'] ≤ Pr[tᵢ ∈ ℰ ∧ t₋ᵢ ∈ ℰ'] ≤ e^{4Δ} · Pr[tᵢ ∈ ℰ] · Pr[t₋ᵢ ∈ ℰ']`.

**Formalization Note.** The paper states the ratio
`Pr[tᵢ ∈ ℰ ∧ t₋ᵢ ∈ ℰ'] / (Pr[tᵢ ∈ ℰ] Pr[t₋ᵢ ∈ ℰ']) ∈ [e^{−4Δ}, e^{4Δ}]`; it is stated here
multiplied out, which is equivalent when `ℰ, ℰ'` are nonempty (the MRF has full support) and
avoids `0/0` for empty sets. `t₋ᵢ` is the restriction of `t` to `{j // j ≠ i}`. -/
theorem lemma_2 {n : ℕ} (G : MRF n) (i : Fin n) (ℰ : Set ℝ≥0)
    (ℰ' : Set ({j : Fin n // j ≠ i} → ℝ≥0))
    (hℰ : ℰ ⊆ (G.A i : Set ℝ≥0)) (hℰ' : ∀ y ∈ ℰ', ∀ j, y j ∈ G.A j.1) :
    Real.exp (-4 * G.maxWeightedDegree) * G.law.prob {t | t i ∈ ℰ} *
        G.law.prob {t | (fun j : {j : Fin n // j ≠ i} => t j.1) ∈ ℰ'} ≤
      G.law.prob {t | t i ∈ ℰ ∧ (fun j : {j : Fin n // j ≠ i} => t j.1) ∈ ℰ'} ∧
    G.law.prob {t | t i ∈ ℰ ∧ (fun j : {j : Fin n // j ≠ i} => t j.1) ∈ ℰ'} ≤
      Real.exp (4 * G.maxWeightedDegree) * G.law.prob {t | t i ∈ ℰ} *
        G.law.prob {t | (fun j : {j : Fin n // j ≠ i} => t j.1) ∈ ℰ'} := by sorry

end SimpleMechMRF
